The prototype relies on several core engineering principles that underpin the operation of its motor control, sensing, navigation, and communication subsystems. This section outlines the theoretical foundations relevant to the design decisions made throughout the project. 

Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) 

The vehicle's four DC motors are controlled using pulse width modulation, a technique in which a digital signal is rapidly switched between high and low states at a fixed frequency. The proportion of time the signal remains high within each cycle is known as the duty cycle, and this determines the average voltage delivered to the motor. The relationship is given by: 

