The trigger pulse remained consistent across all three conditions. The measured pulse amplitude was approximately 3.3V and the pulse width was constant at approximately 10 µs, confirming that the trigger signal generation is independent of object distance and that the micro:bit's GPIO is producing a clean, repeatable output signal. 

 

